  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Imposter 1.0.0 is the first stable release. The package is the same single Imposter package as the 0.2.x line, with the generator and the Imposter.Abstractions runtime inside, and 0.2.27 upgrades to it without code changes.\n\nWhat 1.0.0 commits to\n\nThe public API of Imposter.Abstractions: the GenerateImposter attribute, Arg and the span and out matchers, Count, ImposterMode, IHaveImposterInstance\\<T> with Instance(), and the two exceptions. See the Key API Reference.\n\nThe fluent setup, verification and event API that generated imposters expose, as documented for methods, properties, indexers and events.\n\nThe generator runs on Roslyn 4.0 through 5.0 and emits code for C# 8 through C# 14; every release is tested against all four compiler baselines.\n\nTypeCaster, SpanElementsComparer\\<T> and SetupCollection\\<T> are public because generated imposters call them, but they are hidden from IntelliSense and may change with the generator in the same package.\n\nChanges since 0.2.27\n\nGenerated-code helpers are hidden from IntelliSense (#392, closes #389). TypeCaster and SpanElementsComparer\\<T> carry EditorBrowsable(Never) like SetupCollection\\<T>; the Key API Reference gains an \"Imposter Instance\" section for IHaveImposterInstance\\<T> and Instance().\n\nThe generated \\_lastestInvocationImposter field is now spelled \\_latestInvocationImposter (#394, closes #390). The field is private to the generated class, so nothing changes for callers.",
